// English legal pages: the source text for every non-Hebrew site (the Hebrew version governs).
export default (B) => ({
  updated: "4 November 2026",

  terms: {
    title: "Terms of use and sale",
    lead: "What you get, what it costs, how subscriptions and our Telegram bot work, what you may do with the content and what each side is responsible for.",
    sections: [
      { id: "t-general", h: "About these terms", b: `<p>The ${B.brand} website (youmademyday.store, the "site") is run by ${B.name}, ${B.id}, ${B.addr} ("we", "us"). These terms apply to every use of the site and every purchase on it. By using the site or placing an order, you accept them.</p>
        <p>Our <a href="#privacy">privacy policy</a>, <a href="#refunds">refund policy</a>, <a href="#cookies">cookie policy</a> and <a href="#accessibility">accessibility statement</a> are part of these terms.</p>` },
      { id: "t-seller", h: "Who sells and who made the content", b: `<p>We are the business you deal with on the site. Every course, book and template was written and produced by us, and we own all rights in them. The site is our own store, not a marketplace: there are no other sellers, and no third-party products are sold through it. Payments are processed by our payment provider, which may act as the reseller of the product for the purpose of the payment only (see "Payment").</p>` },
      { id: "t-products", h: "What we sell", b: `<ul><li><b>Digital courses:</b> written lessons with tasks and worksheets, as PDF files to download.</li><li><b>Digital books and printable templates:</b> PDF files to download, read and print.</li><li><b>Bundles:</b> several items together for one price, as listed on the bundle's page.</li><li><b>Subscriptions:</b> the weekly plans Growth and Maximum, whose first day is free, and the monthly plans Spark (a free channel), Good Day, Community and Mentor. Depending on what each paid plan includes: daily messages from our Telegram bot at a time you choose, access to private Telegram groups and channels by topic, access to our library of courses and books, and a personal chat with a member of our team.</li></ul>
        <p>Each product page shows a description, the scope (lessons or pages), the language and the price. What each subscription includes and what it costs is shown on the <a href="#plans">subscriptions page</a>. Covers and previews are illustrations. All products are digital: nothing is shipped.</p>` },
      { id: "t-account", h: "Your account and signing in with Telegram", b: `<p>You don't need an account to browse, read about the products or fill your bag. Accounts on the site are based on Telegram and have no separate password: you sign in through a link that opens our bot in Telegram, or with a 6-digit one-time code that the bot sends you and that is valid for 5 minutes.</p>
        <p>To buy anything, a product or a subscription, you need to sign in with Telegram. That is how we deliver what you bought in the bot and keep it in <a href="#account">your account on the site</a>. We don't ask you for an email address. When you sign in, Telegram gives us only your user ID, name and username and, if Telegram provides them, your language and profile photo. We don't receive your phone number or your chats outside our bot. Full details are in the <a href="#privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
        <p>On the payment page you give the payment provider your payment details and, if you wish, your name. The email address pre-filled there is an internal address of ours, not yours. Keep your Telegram account secure and never share your sign-in code with anyone. Your bag and saved items stay in your own browser (see the <a href="#cookies">cookie policy</a>).</p>` },
      { id: "t-price", h: "Prices and tax", b: `<ul><li>On the Hebrew site, all prices are in Israeli shekels (ILS). On the sites in other languages, the book "Your Maximum" and the weekly plans Growth and Maximum are priced and charged in US dollars (USD), and everything else is in ILS. You are always charged in the currency shown at checkout.</li><li>Courses, books, templates and bundles are paid once. A paid subscription renews automatically every week or every month, as stated on the plan, at the same price until you cancel (see "Subscriptions and automatic renewal"). There are no other recurring charges.</li><li>The price shown is the full price you pay. We add no fees at checkout.</li><li>If you live in Israel, the price includes VAT at the legal rate. Sales to customers living outside Israel are zero-rated for Israeli VAT, so the price is the same and no VAT line is shown.</li><li>Your bank or card issuer may charge its own currency conversion or foreign transaction fees, including when you are charged in US dollars. These are between you and them.</li><li>The binding price is the one shown when you place the order. We may change prices at any time, but a change never affects an order already placed. For subscriptions, a price change applies only as set out in "Subscriptions and automatic renewal".</li><li>If a price or description is obviously wrong (for example, a typing error), we will tell you, cancel the order and refund everything you paid. You may also choose to keep the order at the correct price.</li></ul>` },
      { id: "t-payment", h: "Payment", b: `<p>Payment is by card, through an external, secure payment provider whose payment page opens at checkout. Your card number goes straight to that provider. We never see it and never store it. We work only with a provider that meets the card industry security standard (PCI DSS).</p>
        <p>Our payment provider is the party that charges your card, and it may act as the reseller of the product for the purpose of the payment. Its name may therefore appear on your card statement and on the receipt or invoice for the payment, which you'll find in your account on the site, and it collects and remits sales tax or VAT where it applies. We remain responsible for the product itself, its content, delivery, customer support, cancellations and refunds, under our policies and the law. Our company details shown on the site and in the order details document are those of the business you deal with.</p>
        <p>We may refuse or cancel an order if we reasonably suspect fraud or misuse of a payment card. If we do, any amount charged is refunded in full.</p>` },
      { id: "t-order", h: "How an order is made", b: `<p>You choose products or a subscription, enter your details and pay on the site. Before you pay, the checkout shows the products or the subscription, the total price and these terms. For a subscription it also shows how often you will be charged, that the subscription renews automatically until you cancel, and how to cancel. Payment is taken only after you expressly confirm. For a plan whose first day is free, by confirming you also agree that the first charge is made when the free day ends. The book "Your Maximum" is bought on its own, on its own payment page.</p>
        <p>You buy while signed in with Telegram. The order is complete when the payment is approved. Right after that, our bot sends you a confirmation message in Telegram, and the order appears in <a href="#account">your account on the site</a>.</p>` },
      { id: "t-delivery", h: "Delivery in the bot and in your account", b: `<p>Right after the payment is approved, our Telegram bot sends you a message with your order confirmation, the order details document and the PDF files you bought: courses, books and templates. The same files are also in the library in <a href="#account">your account on the site</a>. We don't send emails to customers. The receipt or invoice for the payment is waiting for you in your account on the site (see "Payment"). With a subscription, the bot adds you to the groups and channels it includes and starts sending your daily messages.</p>
        <p>The order details document is the written disclosure document the law requires. It is sent in the bot message and also kept in <a href="#account">your account on the site</a>, where you can view it and download it as a PDF at any time. It includes our company details, a description of what you bought, the price, the payment details and the cancellation terms. For a subscription, it also states how often you are charged, the automatic renewal and how to cancel.</p>
        <p>We suggest saving the files and the order details document on your device. If the bot message hasn't arrived within an hour, check <a href="#account">your account on the site</a>, or write to us in the bot chat or at ${B.email} and we will send it again. If Telegram is unavailable, everything you bought is waiting in your account, and if you can't reach that either, write to us and we will find another way to get it to you.</p>
        <p class="law">Israeli Consumer Protection Law, 1981, section 14C.</p>` },
      { id: "t-subscriptions", h: "Subscriptions and automatic renewal", b: `<ul><li><b>Renewal:</b> a paid subscription renews automatically every billing period, a week or a month as stated on the plan, at the same price, in the same currency and with the same means of payment, until you cancel. Growth and Maximum renew every week. Spark, Good Day, Community and Mentor renew every month. There is no minimum term.</li><li><b>First day free:</b> on Growth and Maximum you are not charged for the first day. When the free day ends, the first charge is made on the same card, and then every week. Cancelling during the free day stops the charge at once, and you pay nothing at all. The free day is offered once per customer.</li><li><b>Reminder:</b> before every charge, including the first charge at the end of the free day, the bot sends you a reminder with the amount and the charge date.</li><li><b>Library:</b> courses and books included in a subscription are for your personal use while the subscription is active. A product you bought separately stays yours after the subscription ends.</li><li><b>Cancelling:</b> you can cancel at any time, in <a href="#account">your account on the site</a>, by messaging the bot, by email to our company address or by registered mail to our address. Cancellation takes effect within 3 business days at the latest, with no cancellation fee, and from then on no further charge is made. We confirm the cancellation in the bot, and it also appears in your account.</li><li><b>After you cancel:</b> by default your access continues until the end of the billing period you paid for. Cancelling within ${B.refundDays} days of joining refunds your payment for the current billing period in full, and you can also ask to end the subscription at once with a pro-rata refund. Details are in the <a href="#refunds">refund policy</a>.</li><li><b>Changes to price or content:</b> we will tell you in the bot and in your account at least 30 days before any change to a subscription's price or to what it includes. The change applies only from the first charge after the notice period ends, and you can cancel before then at no cost. Where the law requires your consent to the change, we will ask for it, and without it the subscription will not renew at the new price.</li><li><b>A failed charge:</b> we will tell you in the bot and let you update your means of payment. If the payment is not completed, the subscription ends.</li><li><b>When a subscription ends</b>, for any reason, the daily messages stop and your access to its private groups and channels is removed.</li><li><b>Spark</b> is a free channel: there is no charge, and you can leave it at any time.</li><li><b>Discontinuing a service:</b> if we decide to stop a particular subscription or the whole service, we will tell you in advance, stop charging you and refund the unused part of any billing period you paid for.</li></ul>
        <p class="law">Israeli Consumer Protection Law, 1981, sections 13D1 and 14C.</p>` },
      { id: "t-cancel", h: "Cancellation and refunds", b: `<p>Courses can be cancelled for a full refund within ${B.refundDays} days. Books and templates can be cancelled within ${B.refundDays} days if they have not been downloaded yet. Subscriptions can be cancelled at any time. Cancelling during the free day of a weekly plan costs nothing, and cancelling within ${B.refundDays} days of joining refunds your payment for the current billing period in full. All details, including bundles and the rules for customers in the EU and the UK, are in our <a href="#refunds">refund policy</a>. A "Cancel an order" link appears at the bottom of every page, and you can also write to our Telegram bot.</p>` },
      { id: "t-license", h: "Your licence to use the content", b: `<p>When you buy a product, you get a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use it for yourself. You may:</p>
        <ul><li>keep copies on your own devices and print them for your own use;</li><li>fill in templates and use them in your own work or business, for example a planner for your clients or a budget sheet for your shop.</li></ul>
        <p>A subscription gives you personal access to its content for as long as it is active. The licence and the access are for one person. If you want to use a product with a team or a class, write to us first.</p>` },
      { id: "t-prohibited", h: "What you may not do", b: `<ul><li>Share, send, sell, rent, lend or publish the files or the subscription content (the daily messages and what is posted in our groups and channels), or any part of them, including in other groups, drives or file-sharing services.</li><li>Pass on access to your account, your subscription or our groups to anyone else.</li><li>Resell or give away the templates themselves, even edited, or offer them as your own templates.</li><li>Use the content to build a course, workshop, book or other product of your own.</li><li>Remove our name, copyright notices or other marks from the files.</li><li>Use the content to train or fine-tune artificial intelligence models, or feed whole files into such systems to reproduce them.</li><li>Copy the site by automated means, try to break its security, or use it in a way that harms it or other users.</li></ul>
        <p>Using the content in breach of these terms ends your licence, without affecting any other right we have under the law.</p>` },
      { id: "t-telegram", h: "Telegram, our groups and community rules", b: `<p>Our bot, channels and groups run on Telegram, a third-party platform (Telegram Messenger Inc. and Telegram FZ-LLC). We are not affiliated with Telegram, and Telegram does not sponsor or endorse our service. Your use of Telegram is subject to Telegram's own terms of service and privacy policy. Telegram's availability is outside our control. If it is unavailable, what you bought is available in your account on the site.</p>
        <p>In our groups and channels:</p>
        <ul><li>write respectfully, with no insults, harassment, incitement, or offensive or sexual content;</li><li>don't post advertising, self-promotion or spam;</li><li>don't share paid content, other members' messages or their personal details outside the group;</li><li>don't ask other members for money or personal information.</li></ul>
        <p>We may delete messages and remove from our groups anyone who breaks these rules. For a serious or repeated breach, we may also end the subscription, and we will then refund the unused part of any billing period you paid for. What you write in a group is visible to its other members. Messages written by other members are theirs, not ours, but we will deal with every report of a message that breaks the rules.</p>
        <p>Content in our groups, channels, daily messages and the Mentor chat is general learning and inspiration, not professional advice (see "Learning content, not professional advice").</p>` },
      { id: "t-ip", h: "Intellectual property and trademarks", b: `<p>All content on the site and in the products, including texts, lessons, books, templates, design, illustrations, the name ${B.brand} and our logo, belongs to ${B.name} and is protected by copyright and trademark law.</p>
        <p>Names of other products and services mentioned in our guides, such as ChatGPT, Claude, Canva, Excel, Google Sheets, Instagram, LinkedIn and CapCut, are trademarks of their owners. We use them only to describe what our guides teach. We are not affiliated with these companies, and they do not sponsor or endorse our products.</p>
        <p>If you believe something on the site infringes your rights, write to ${B.email} with your details, the material in question, where it appears and the right you believe is infringed. We will look into it promptly and, where justified, remove or change it.</p>
        <p class="law">Israeli Copyright Act, 2007; Trademarks Ordinance [New Version], 1972.</p>` },
      { id: "t-advice", h: "Learning content, not professional advice", b: `<p>Our products, the daily messages, the content in our groups and channels and the Mentor chat are for learning and general information. They are not medical, nutritional, psychological, legal, tax or financial advice, and they don't replace a professional who knows your situation. Results depend on you, and we don't promise any particular outcome, income or saving.</p>
        <ul><li><b>Recipes</b> list the main allergens, but check every ingredient yourself against your own allergies and needs.</li><li><b>Running, yoga and other exercise books</b> are written for healthy beginners. Check with a doctor before you start, and stop if you feel pain or discomfort.</li><li>Before a significant change to your health, diet, money or legal matters, talk to a qualified professional.</li><li><b>The Mentor chat</b> is personal learning support, not therapy or professional advice. If you are in distress or in an emergency, contact a professional or the emergency services.</li></ul>` },
      { id: "t-liability", h: "Our responsibility", b: `<p>We work hard to keep the site and the products accurate and available, but the site is offered as is and may sometimes be unavailable or contain errors. Our bot, groups and site sign-in also depend on Telegram being available. If it isn't, what you bought is in your account, and if you can't reach that either, we will help you get it another way. If a product is faulty, we will fix it, replace it or refund you, as set out in the <a href="#refunds">refund policy</a>.</p>
        <p>As far as the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, and our total liability for any product is limited to the amount you paid for it. This limit does not apply to harm caused on purpose or by gross negligence, to bodily injury, or where the law does not allow liability to be limited. Nothing in these terms reduces the rights you have as a consumer under the law.</p>` },
      { id: "t-minors", h: "Age", b: `<p>You must be 18 or older to buy on the site. Anyone under 18 may buy only with the consent of a parent or legal guardian, who is responsible for the purchase.</p>` },
      { id: "t-changes", h: "Changes to these terms", b: `<p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date of the latest update appears at the top of the page. A change never applies to an order already placed: each order is governed by the terms in force when it was made. We will announce significant changes on the site before they take effect. For subscriptions, a significant change to these terms applies only from the first charge after we announce it; we will tell you in the bot and in your account at least 30 days in advance, and you can cancel before it applies.</p>
        <p>If a clause in these terms is found invalid, the rest stays in force.</p>` },
      { id: "t-law", h: "Governing law and courts", b: `<p>These terms and every purchase on the site are governed by the laws of the State of Israel. The competent courts in the Haifa district have jurisdiction.</p>
        <p>This does not take away your right to bring a claim in another court where the law allows it, including a small claims court near where you live. If you live outside Israel, for example in the EU or the UK, you also keep the protection of the mandatory consumer laws of your country of residence, and you may bring proceedings in your country where that law gives you the right.</p>` },
      { id: "t-language", h: "Languages", b: `<p>The site is offered in several languages for your convenience. The Hebrew version of these terms and policies is the official one. If a translation differs from it, the Hebrew version governs, unless the law of your country requires otherwise. Where a term is unclear, it is read in your favour.</p>` },
      { id: "t-contact", h: "Contact us", b: `<p>${B.name}</p><p>${B.id}</p><p>${B.addr}</p><p>Email: <a href="mailto:${B.email}">${B.email}</a></p><p>Telegram: in the chat with our bot, where our team answers</p><p>Service hours: ${B.hours}</p>` },
    ],
  },

  privacy: {
    title: "Privacy policy",
    lead: "What personal data we collect, why, who receives it, how long we keep it and how you control it.",
    sections: [
      { id: "p-controller", h: "Who is responsible for your data", b: `<p>${B.name}, ${B.id}, ${B.addr}, is the controller of the personal data collected through the site (the "database owner" under Israeli law). For any privacy question or request, write to <a href="mailto:${B.email}">${B.email}</a>.</p>
        <p>We collect as little as we need to sell you digital products and subscriptions, to run our bot and community on Telegram and to meet our legal duties.</p>` },
      { id: "p-laws", h: "Which laws apply", b: `<p>We handle personal data under the Israeli Protection of Privacy Law, 1981, including Amendment 13, in force since August 2025, and the Protection of Privacy (Data Security) Regulations, 2017. If you are in the European Union, the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) or the UK GDPR also applies when we offer you our products, and this policy gives you the information those laws require.</p>` },
      { id: "p-collect", h: "What we collect and where it comes from", b: `<ul><li><b>From Telegram, when you sign in or contact our bot:</b> your Telegram user ID, name and username and, if Telegram provides them, your language and profile photo. We don't receive your phone number, your contacts or any chats outside our bot.</li><li><b>From your account and orders:</b> an internal customer number we assign to you, your orders, subscriptions, receipts and order details documents. We don't collect an email address from you.</li><li><b>From you, in the bot and in customer support:</b> the messages you send to the bot, your conversations with our support team, the Mentor chat if you have that plan, and the time you chose for your daily messages, with your time zone.</li><li><b>From you, if you choose to email us:</b> your email address and what you write, only to answer you.</li><li><b>Subscription and community records:</b> which plan you chose, when you joined, your free day, your weekly or monthly charges, the reminders we sent, cancellations, and which of our groups and channels you belong to through your subscription. Messages you write in our groups are visible to us as the groups' admins.</li><li><b>From the payment provider:</b> we give the payment provider an internal email address of ours, pre-filled on the payment page, not yours. On that page you give it your billing country and payment details and, if you wish, your name. It passes us confirmation that the payment was approved, the amount, a transaction number and, sometimes, the card type and its last four digits. For subscriptions, also the charge dates and whether a charge failed. We never receive your full card number.</li><li><b>From your use of the products:</b> what you bought and when, and whether and when each file was delivered or downloaded. We need this to deliver the files and to apply the <a href="#refunds">refund policy</a>.</li><li><b>Signing in to the site:</b> a one-time code sent by the bot (valid for 5 minutes) and a sign-in token that links your browser to your account.</li><li><b>Technical data:</b> when you visit, our site hosting provider automatically receives standard server data, such as your IP address, browser type and the page requested. We don't receive or use these logs. When you sign in or use the bot, our server receives basic technical data, such as your IP address and the time of the request, and uses it only for security and to prevent abuse.</li></ul>
        <p>Your bag and saved items are stored only in your own browser and are never sent to us. The sign-in token is stored in your browser and sent only to our server, to recognise that you are signed in. We use no analytics tools, no advertising cookies and no tracking pixels. See the <a href="#cookies">cookie policy</a>.</p>` },
      { id: "p-purposes", h: "Why we use it, and on what legal basis", b: `<div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Data</th><th>Legal basis under the GDPR</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Processing your order, delivering the files in the bot and in your account, and keeping your receipts and order details document</td><td>Telegram ID, name, customer number, order and download details</td><td>Performing our contract with you</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Signing you in and identifying your account</td><td>Telegram data, one-time code, sign-in token</td><td>Performing our contract with you</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Managing your subscription, the free day, weekly or monthly charges, reminders before each charge and cancellations</td><td>Subscription records, payment details, Telegram ID and customer number</td><td>Performing our contract with you, and a legal obligation (consumer law)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sending your daily messages at the time you chose</td><td>Telegram ID, plan, time and time zone</td><td>Performing our contract with you</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Adding you to groups and channels, removing you when the subscription ends, and running the community under its rules</td><td>Telegram ID, membership records, messages in groups</td><td>Performing our contract with you, and our legitimate interest in keeping the community safe</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Customer support and the Mentor chat</td><td>Bot messages, support conversations, and emails if you choose to write</td><td>Performing our contract with you</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Keeping accounting records</td><td>Name, order and payment details</td><td>A legal obligation (tax and accounting law)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Handling cancellations, refunds and complaints</td><td>Order and download details, your messages</td><td>Our contract with you and our legal obligations under consumer law</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Preventing fraud and keeping the site secure</td><td>Payment details, technical data</td><td>Our legitimate interest in protecting customers and the business</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Defending or making legal claims</td><td>Order records and correspondence</td><td>Our legitimate interest in protecting our legal rights</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sending news and offers</td><td>Telegram ID and name</td><td>Your consent only, which you can withdraw at any time</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
        <p>We don't sell personal data, don't use it for advertising profiles and don't make decisions about you by purely automated means. The payment provider may run its own automated fraud checks on card payments.</p>` },
      { id: "p-duty", h: "Do you have to give us this data?", b: `<p>No law requires you to give us personal data. It is up to you. But without signing in with Telegram and a means of payment, you cannot buy a product or subscription and we cannot deliver it. No email address is needed. Writing to us is always optional.</p>
        <p class="law">Israeli Protection of Privacy Law, 1981, section 11; GDPR, article 13.</p>` },
      { id: "p-recipients", h: "Who receives the data", b: `<p>We share personal data only as far as needed, and only with:</p>
        <ul><li><b>Our payment provider</b>, which receives our internal email address (not yours), your name if you gave it, your billing country and your payment details to process the payment, and may act as the reseller of the product for the payment. For the payment, it acts under its own privacy policy as an independent controller, not on our behalf.</li><li><b>Service providers who work for us:</b> our company email provider (Google), for messages you choose to email us, our site hosting provider (GitHub), the cloud hosting provider that runs the server for our bot and sign-in system, and our accountant. They may use the data only to provide their service, and must protect it.</li><li><b>Telegram</b>, as the platform our bot, messages, groups and channels run on. Telegram handles data under its own privacy policy, as an independent party and not on our behalf.</li><li><b>Other group members</b> see your Telegram name, username and profile photo and what you write in the group (see "Telegram and what others can see").</li><li><b>Authorities</b>, when the law or a court order requires it.</li><li><b>A buyer of the business</b>, if the business is sold or merged, under the same commitments as in this policy.</li></ul>` },
      { id: "p-telegram", h: "Telegram and what others can see", b: `<ul><li>Chats with our bot and with customer support are ordinary Telegram cloud chats, not end-to-end encrypted chats. They pass through Telegram's servers and are also stored by us, as set out in "How long we keep it".</li><li>In our groups, other members see your name, username and profile photo, as you set them in Telegram, and the messages you write. You can choose what is shown in Telegram's privacy settings.</li><li>You can delete messages you wrote with Telegram's own tools. We delete what we store, but we cannot delete data from Telegram's servers or from other people's devices beyond what Telegram allows.</li></ul>` },
      { id: "p-transfers", h: "Transfers outside your country", b: `<p>We are based in Israel. The European Commission and the United Kingdom recognise Israel as giving personal data an adequate level of protection, so data may flow from the EU, the EEA and the UK to us without extra steps.</p>
        <p>Telegram stores data on its own servers outside Israel, under its own privacy policy. Using our bot and groups means your data passes through them.</p>
        <p>Some of our service providers, including the cloud hosting provider of our server, also store data on servers outside Israel, including in the United States. We use providers that protect the data with recognised safeguards, such as the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework or standard contractual clauses, and we transfer data from Israel only as the Israeli transfer regulations allow.</p>
        <p class="law">Protection of Privacy (Transfer of Data to Databases Abroad) Regulations, 2001; GDPR, chapter V.</p>` },
      { id: "p-retention", h: "How long we keep it", b: `<ul><li><b>Orders, payment records and subscription records (including charges and cancellations):</b> 7 years from the end of the tax year, as Israeli tax law requires.</li><li><b>Download and delivery records:</b> together with the order they belong to.</li><li><b>Your Telegram account details and chosen message time:</b> as long as your account is active. After you delete your account, they are deleted within 30 days, except what the law requires us to keep.</li><li><b>Bot messages, support and Mentor conversations, and emails:</b> up to 24 months from the last message, unless we need them longer for a claim.</li><li><b>Group and channel membership:</b> as long as the subscription is active. When it ends, you are removed from the groups, and the record is kept with the subscription records.</li><li><b>One-time sign-in code:</b> valid for 5 minutes, and deleted once used or expired.</li><li><b>Sign-in token:</b> until you sign out or it expires.</li><li><b>Technical data on our server:</b> up to 90 days, unless needed to investigate a security incident.</li><li><b>Marketing consent and unsubscribe records:</b> as long as you are on the list, and afterwards only as long as needed to prove consent or respect your opt-out.</li></ul>
        <p>When data is no longer needed, we delete it or make it anonymous.</p>` },
      { id: "p-security", h: "How we protect it", b: `<p>The site and our server run over an encrypted connection (HTTPS). The sign-in code works once and is valid for 5 minutes only. Access to personal data is limited to those who need it, accounts are protected with strong passwords and two-step verification, and we choose service providers who maintain a high level of security. Our security measures follow the Protection of Privacy (Data Security) Regulations, 2017. If a serious security incident happens, we will report it to the authorities and inform those affected, as the law requires.</p>
        <p>No system is perfectly secure, so please tell us at once at ${B.email} if you suspect a problem.</p>` },
      { id: "p-rights", h: "Your rights", b: `<p><b>Under Israeli law</b>, you may:</p>
        <ul><li>see the personal data we hold about you (section 13 of the Protection of Privacy Law);</li><li>ask us to correct, complete or delete data that is wrong, incomplete, unclear or out of date (section 14);</li><li>ask to be removed from any mailing list (section 17F).</li></ul>
        <p><b>If you are in the EU, the EEA or the UK</b>, you also have the right to:</p>
        <ul><li>get access to your data and a copy of it;</li><li>have it corrected;</li><li>have it erased;</li><li>restrict how we use it;</li><li>receive it in a common, machine-readable format, or have it sent to someone else (portability);</li><li>object to its use based on our legitimate interests;</li><li>withdraw your consent at any time, without affecting what was done before.</li></ul>
        <p>Some rights have legal limits. For example, we must keep order and payment records for the period tax law sets, even if you ask us to delete them.</p>
        <p><b>Deleting your account:</b> send the command /delete to our bot, or email us. Deleting your account ends any active subscription with no further charges, removes you from our groups and channels, and deletes your account details and the conversations we store, except what the law requires us to keep, such as order and payment records. You can change the time of your daily messages, or stop them, in the bot at any time.</p>
        <p>To use any of these rights, write to ${B.email} or in the bot chat. We may ask you to confirm it is really you, and we will answer within 30 days. Using your rights is free.</p>` },
      { id: "p-complaints", h: "Complaints", b: `<p>If you are unhappy with how we handle your data, please tell us first and we'll try to fix it. You may also complain to:</p>
        <ul><li>the Privacy Protection Authority in the Israeli Ministry of Justice;</li><li>if you are in the EU or the EEA, the data protection supervisory authority in the country where you live or work, or where the problem happened;</li><li>if you are in the UK, the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO).</li></ul>` },
      { id: "p-marketing", h: "Marketing messages in the bot", b: `<p>We don't send emails to customers. We send news and offers in the bot only to people who agreed to receive them, in a separate consent that is not pre-ticked. In the bot you can opt out with a message, and you can also opt out by writing to us. Service messages, such as the order confirmation, the products themselves, your subscription's daily messages, the reminder before each charge and cancellation confirmations, are part of the service and are sent even without marketing consent.</p>
        <p class="law">Israeli Communications (Telecommunications and Broadcasting) Law, 1982, section 30A.</p>` },
      { id: "p-children", h: "Children", b: `<p>The site is meant for adults. We don't knowingly collect personal data from children under 16 without a parent's or guardian's consent. If you think a child has given us data, write to us and we will delete it.</p>` },
      { id: "p-changes", h: "Changes to this policy", b: `<p>If we change this policy significantly, for example by starting to use a new kind of tool or a new purpose, we will announce it on the site before the change takes effect and, where the law requires, ask for your consent. The date of the latest update appears at the top of the page.</p>` },
      { id: "p-contact", h: "Contact for privacy", b: `<p>${B.name}, ${B.addr}</p><p>Email: <a href="mailto:${B.email}">${B.email}</a></p><p>Telegram: in the chat with our bot</p><p>Service hours: ${B.hours}</p>` },
    ],
  },

  refunds: {
    title: "Refund and cancellation policy",
    lead: "What you can cancel, until when, how much comes back and how to do it.",
    cancelIntro: `To cancel, use <a href="#account">your account on the site</a>, send this text as a message to our Telegram bot or to our company email <b>${B.email}</b>, or write in your own words. No reason is needed. We'll confirm your cancellation in the bot, and it will also appear in your account.`,
    cancelText: `Hello,
I would like to cancel my order.
Full name:
Telegram username:
Order or customer number (if known):
Product(s) or subscription I am cancelling:
Date of purchase or joining:`,
    sections: [
      { id: "r-summary", h: "In short", b: `<div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Cancel until</th><th>What comes back</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><b>Digital course</b></td><td>${B.refundDays} days from purchase</td><td>A full refund</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Book or template, not downloaded</b></td><td>${B.refundDays} days from purchase</td><td>A full refund</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Book or template, downloaded</b></td><td>No cancellation</td><td>Only if the file is faulty and we can't fix it</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Bundle</b></td><td>${B.refundDays} days from purchase</td><td>The share of the items not yet downloaded</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Weekly plan, during the free day</b></td><td>Until the end of the first day</td><td>No charge at all</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Paid subscription, weekly or monthly, at the start</b></td><td>${B.refundDays} days from joining</td><td>Your whole payment for the current billing period</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Paid subscription, later</b></td><td>Any time</td><td>Future charges stop. If you ask to end it at once: the pro-rata share of the billing period</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
        <p>We charge no cancellation fee, and refunds are paid within ${B.payoutDays} days. A refund is always the amount you actually paid for the item.</p>` },
      { id: "r-courses", h: "Courses", b: `<p>You can cancel a course within ${B.refundDays} days of the purchase, or of the day you received the order details document in the bot if that came later, and get all your money back, even if you have already started the course.</p>` },
      { id: "r-books", h: "Books and templates (PDF)", b: `<p>A digital book or template is computer information. Under Israeli law, a purchase of it can't be cancelled once it has been delivered. That is why:</p>
        <ul><li><b>Before the first download:</b> you can cancel within ${B.refundDays} days and get a full refund.</li><li><b>After a download:</b> the purchase can't be cancelled.</li><li><b>A faulty file, a missing file or one that doesn't match its description:</b> see "Faulty products" below. This is always fixed or refunded.</li></ul>
        <p>Every book has a free preview on its page, so you can see what you get before you buy.</p>` },
      { id: "r-bundles", h: "Bundles", b: `<p>You can cancel a bundle within ${B.refundDays} days. We refund the part of the bundle price that belongs to the items you have not downloaded, according to each item's share of the bundle's regular total price. Courses in a bundle follow the course rule. If you have not downloaded anything, you get the full bundle price back.</p>` },
      { id: "r-subscriptions", h: "Subscriptions", b: `<ul><li><b>Cancel any time:</b> in <a href="#account">your account on the site</a>, by messaging our Telegram bot, by email to ${B.email} or by registered mail to our address, ${B.addr}. You don't need to give a reason, and there is no cancellation fee.</li><li><b>When it takes effect:</b> within 3 business days at the latest of receiving your notice. From then on no further charge is made, and we confirm the cancellation in the bot, and it also appears in your account.</li><li><b>During the free day</b> of Growth or Maximum: cancelling stops the charge at once, and you pay nothing at all.</li><li><b>Within ${B.refundDays} days of joining:</b> cancelling refunds your payment for the current billing period in full, even if you have already started receiving messages or taking part in the groups. On a monthly plan, this is your whole first payment. On a weekly plan, it is the payment for the current week; a week that has already ended was used in full.</li><li><b>After the ${B.refundDays} days:</b> by default your access continues until the end of the billing period you paid for, and the subscription then ends with no further charge. Want it to end at once? Say so in your cancellation message: your access will end, and we will refund the pro-rata share of the billing period for the days left.</li><li><b>A weekly or monthly renewal</b> doesn't start a new ${B.refundDays}-day period, but you can cancel at any time as described here.</li><li><b>When the subscription ends</b>, the daily messages stop and your access to the private groups and channels is removed.</li><li><b>Spark</b> is a free channel with no charge, and you can leave it at any time.</li></ul>
        <p class="law">Israeli Consumer Protection Law, 1981, sections 13D1 and 14C.</p>` },
      { id: "r-how", h: "How to cancel", b: `<p>Any clear message is enough, in writing or by speaking with us. You don't need to give a reason. The easiest ways are the cancel button in <a href="#account">your account on the site</a> or a message to our Telegram bot. You can also email our company address ${B.email} using the text above. Please include your Telegram username and order number, so we can find the order or subscription. We will confirm every cancellation in the bot, and it will also appear in your account.</p>` },
      { id: "r-money", h: "When the money comes back", b: `<ul><li>Within ${B.payoutDays} days of receiving your cancellation, to the same means of payment you used, through our payment provider. This also applies to subscription refunds.</li><li>Your card issuer shows the credit according to its own billing dates.</li><li>We cancel the charge in full: no cancellation fee and no handling fee.</li></ul>` },
      { id: "r-extended", h: "Seniors, people with disabilities and new immigrants", b: `<p>If you are 65 or older, a person with a disability, or a new immigrant (up to 5 years from receiving an immigrant certificate or entitlement), and the purchase included a conversation with us, by phone or otherwise, you may cancel within 4 months instead of ${B.refundDays} days. The rule for books and templates that were already downloaded applies here too. We may ask for a document that shows your eligibility.</p>
        <p class="law">Israeli Consumer Protection Law, 1981, section 14C1.</p>` },
      { id: "r-defects", h: "Faulty products", b: `<p>If a file is faulty, missing, won't open or doesn't match its description, tell us. We'll fix it or send a working copy quickly. If we can't, you get a full refund for that item, whether or not you downloaded it, and with no fee. Your legal rights for faulty digital content are never affected.</p>` },
      { id: "r-eu", h: "Customers in the EU and the UK", b: `<p>If you live in the European Union or the United Kingdom, you have a 14-day right of withdrawal from the day of purchase, without giving a reason.</p>
        <ul><li><b>Courses:</b> our ${B.refundDays}-day full refund applies even after you start, so you keep that right in full.</li><li><b>Books and templates:</b> at checkout we will ask you to expressly agree that the download may start right away, and to confirm that you know you lose the right of withdrawal once you download. We confirm this in the order details document. After you download, the purchase can't be withdrawn. If you haven't downloaded the file, or if you didn't give that consent, you can withdraw within 14 days for a full refund.</li><li><b>Subscriptions:</b> at checkout we will ask you to expressly request that the service start right away. Cancelling during the free day costs nothing. Withdrawing within 14 days of joining refunds your payment for the current billing period in full, which is more than the law requires, since it allows a charge for the part already provided. A weekly or monthly renewal doesn't start a new withdrawal period, and you can cancel at any time as described under "Subscriptions".</li><li>To withdraw, send any clear statement, for example the text above.</li></ul>
        <p class="law">EU Consumer Rights Directive 2011/83/EU, articles 9, 14(3) and 16(m); UK Consumer Contracts (Information, Cancellation and Additional Charges) Regulations 2013.</p>` },
      { id: "r-law", h: "The law, and which rule wins", b: `<ul><li>Israeli Consumer Protection Law, 1981, sections 13D1, 14C, 14C1 and 14E</li><li>Consumer Protection (Cancellation of Transaction) Regulations, 2010</li></ul>
        <p>If our policy is better for you than the law, our policy applies. If the law, including the law of your country, gives you more, the law applies.</p>` },
    ],
  },

  cookies: {
    title: "Cookie and local storage policy",
    lead: "What the site stores in your browser, why, and how to clear it.",
    sections: [
      { id: "c-what", h: "What we store", b: `<p>The site uses no advertising or tracking cookies. It keeps up to three small items in your browser, in local storage or, for signing in, in a strictly necessary cookie:</p>
        <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>What it holds</th><th>How long</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><b>ymd-cart</b></td><td>The products in your bag</td><td>Until you empty the bag or clear your browser data</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>ymd-wish</b></td><td>The products you saved</td><td>Until you remove them or clear your browser data</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>ymd-session</b></td><td>A sign-in token showing that you signed in with Telegram, with no name, phone number or message content</td><td>Until you sign out, it expires or you clear your browser data</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
        <p>All three are strictly necessary for features you ask for. Your bag and saved items stay on your device and are never sent to us or to anyone else. The sign-in token is sent only to our server, to recognise that you are signed in, and to no one else.</p>` },
      { id: "c-none", h: "What we don't use", b: `<ul><li>No analytics or statistics tools.</li><li>No advertising cookies and no tracking pixels.</li><li>No social media plugins.</li><li>No external fonts: our fonts are served from our own site, so loading a page doesn't contact Google Fonts or any other font service.</li></ul>` },
      { id: "c-third", h: "Third parties", b: `<ul><li><b>Hosting:</b> the site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web server, GitHub receives standard technical data, such as your IP address, when your browser loads a page, and handles it under its own privacy statement. We don't receive these logs.</li><li><b>Payment:</b> when checkout opens, the external payment provider's payment page may set its own cookies, for example for security and fraud prevention. Those cookies are covered by the provider's own policy. We will update this page when checkout opens.</li><li><b>Telegram:</b> the sign-in, join and support buttons open links to t.me or telegram.org, or the Telegram app. These are third-party services that may store their own cookies or data under Telegram's privacy policy. Our site does not load any Telegram plugin or script on its pages.</li></ul>` },
      { id: "c-clear", h: "How to clear them", b: `<p>Emptying your bag and removing your saved items clears their contents, and signing out deletes the sign-in token. To delete everything the site stores, clear the site data for youmademyday.store in your browser's privacy or site settings. Private browsing windows delete it automatically when closed. The site works without this storage too, but your bag won't be remembered between visits, and you will need to sign in again each visit.</p>` },
      { id: "c-consent", h: "Why there is no cookie banner", b: `<p>The law requires consent for storing information on your device unless it is strictly necessary for a service you asked for. We store only what is strictly necessary, so no consent banner is needed. If we ever add anything else, we will ask for your consent first and update this page.</p>
        <p class="law">EU ePrivacy Directive 2002/58/EC, article 5(3); UK Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations 2003.</p>` },
      { id: "c-more", h: "More information", b: `<p>How we handle personal data is explained in our <a href="#privacy">privacy policy</a>. Questions: ${B.email}.</p>` },
    ],
  },

  accessibility: {
    title: "Accessibility statement",
    lead: "How we make the site usable for everyone, what is still limited and how to get help.",
    sections: [
      { id: "a-commitment", h: "Our commitment", b: `<p>We want everyone, including people with disabilities, to be able to browse the site, read about the products and buy them independently and with dignity. Accessibility is part of how we design and build the site, not something added at the end.</p>` },
      { id: "a-standard", h: "The standard we follow", b: `<p>The site was built to meet Israeli Standard IS 5568, which is based on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.0 at level AA, and we aim for WCAG 2.1 level AA. We keep checking and improving it as we add pages and products.</p>
        <p class="law">Israeli Equal Rights for Persons with Disabilities (Service Accessibility Adjustments) Regulations, 2013, regulation 35.</p>` },
      { id: "a-done", h: "What we have done", b: `<ul><li><b>Keyboard:</b> every link, button and menu can be reached and used with the keyboard, and a "skip to content" link appears first on every page.</li><li><b>Visible focus:</b> a clear outline shows where you are as you move with the keyboard.</li><li><b>Screen readers:</b> buttons and icons have text labels, decorative icons are hidden from assistive technology, and book covers are made of real text, so their titles can be read aloud.</li><li><b>Structure:</b> pages use proper headings and lists, so you can move around by heading.</li><li><b>Colour and contrast:</b> text and background colours were chosen to meet the AA contrast level, and colour is never the only way information is shown.</li><li><b>Text size:</b> text can be enlarged up to 200% with the browser's zoom without losing content or function, and the layout adapts to small screens.</li><li><b>Motion:</b> when your device is set to reduce motion, animations and the 3D effects are switched off. When it is set to reduce transparency, see-through backgrounds become solid.</li><li><b>Language and direction:</b> each language site declares its language, and pages read right to left in Hebrew and Arabic and left to right in the other languages.</li><li><b>Our Telegram bot:</b> the bot's messages are written mostly as plain text, and its buttons have text labels, so they can be read with your device's screen reader in the Telegram apps.</li></ul>` },
      { id: "a-limits", h: "Known limitations", b: `<ul><li>The decorative 3D animations on some pages are not accessible to everyone. They carry no information, and they are switched off when your device asks to reduce motion.</li><li>The PDF products may not be fully tagged for screen readers. If you need an accessible version of a product you bought or want to buy, such as a tagged PDF or a text file, write to us and we'll prepare one at no extra cost.</li><li>When checkout opens, payment takes place on the external payment provider's page, which we don't control. If you have difficulty there, contact us and we'll help you complete the purchase.</li><li>The Telegram apps are not under our control, and their accessibility depends on Telegram. If you have trouble receiving a product or a message in the bot, everything is also in your account on the site, and you can ask us for another format that suits you.</li></ul>
        <p>If you find anything else that is hard to use, please tell us.</p>` },
      { id: "a-help", h: "How to ask for help", b: `<p>If you have trouble using the site or a product, or you need information in an accessible format, write to us at <a href="mailto:${B.email}">${B.email}</a> or in the chat with our Telegram bot. Please describe the problem, the page or product, and, if you can, the browser and assistive technology you use. We will reply as soon as possible and help you find a solution.</p>` },
      { id: "a-coordinator", h: "Accessibility contact", b: `<p>${B.name}</p><p>Email: <a href="mailto:${B.email}">${B.email}</a></p><p>Telegram: in the chat with our bot</p><p>Address: ${B.addr}</p><p>Service hours: ${B.hours}</p>` },
      { id: "a-date", h: "Date of this statement", b: `<p>This statement was last updated on 4 November 2026.</p>` },
    ],
  },
});
